<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply off $1.5 bln in Sept 30 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply off $1.5 bln in Sept 30 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply fell $1.5 billion in the September 30 week to $3,758.8 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure fell $3.8 billion to $4,774.5 billion. M-1 rose $2.4 billion to $1,090.5 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,765.7 billion versus $3,765.0 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
</text>
